<title>USA: Cedar Hill, Texas, obligations at 5.25 pct in 2001.</title>
<headline>Cedar Hill, Texas, obligations at 5.25 pct in 2001.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co said Tuesday it tentatively priced $675,000 Cedar Hill Independent School District, Texas, public property finance contractual obligations at a top yield of 5.25 percent in 2001.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:  </p>
<p>PUBLIC PROPERTY FINANCE CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS</p>
<p>RE: $675,000*</p>
<p>SERIES 1996</p>
<p>CEDAR HILL INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT</p>
<p>(DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS)</p>
<p>  MOODY'S: NAF		   S&amp;P: NAF		   FITCH: BBB</p>
<p>  DATED: 08/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 02/15/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 08/15</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>08/15/1997		  100M    4.30  %	  4.40</p>
<p>						   (Approx. $ Price 99.909)</p>
<p>08/15/1998		  100M    4.60  %	  4.70</p>
<p>						   (Approx. $ Price 99.816)</p>
<p>08/15/1999		  100M    4.80  %	  4.90</p>
<p>						   (Approx. $ Price 99.728)</p>
<p>08/15/2000		  175M    5.00  %	  5.10</p>
<p>						   (Approx. $ Price 99.645)</p>
<p>08/15/2001		  200M    5.20  %	  5.25</p>
<p>						   (Approx. $ Price 99.781)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Thursday, August 29, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on September 26, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>Rauscher Pierce Refsnes, Inc.</p>
<p>Pryor, McClendon, Counts &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
